    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.8 RHEL-09-211045"
      info        : "The systemd Ctrl-Alt-Delete burst key sequence in RHEL 9 must be disabled.

GROUP ID: V-257784
RULE ID: SV-257784r1044832

A locally logged-on user who presses Ctrl-Alt-Delete when at the console can reboot the system. If accidentally pressed, as could happen in the case of a mixed OS environment, this can create the risk of short-term loss of availability of systems due to unintentional reboot. In a graphical user environment, risk of unintentional reboot from the Ctrl-Alt-Delete sequence is reduced because the user will be prompted before any action is taken.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"
      solution    : "Configure the system to disable the CtrlAltDelBurstAction by added or modifying the following line in the \"/etc/systemd/system.conf\" configuration file:

CtrlAltDelBurstAction=none

Reload the daemon for this change to take effect.

$ sudo systemctl daemon-reload"
