      info        : "The x86 Ctrl-Alt-Delete key sequence must be disabled on RHEL 9.

GROUP ID: V-257785
RULE ID: SV-257785r1044833

A locally logged-on user who presses Ctrl-Alt-Delete when at the console can reboot the system. If accidentally pressed, as could happen in the case of a mixed OS environment, this can create the risk of short-term loss of availability of systems due to unintentional reboot. In a graphical user environment, risk of unintentional reboot from the Ctrl-Alt-Delete sequence is reduced because the user will be prompted before any action is taken.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 9 to disable the ctrl-alt-del.target with the following command:

$ sudo systemctl disable --now ctrl-alt-del.target
$ sudo systemctl mask --now ctrl-alt-del.target"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.7,800-171r3|03.01.07a.,800-53|AC-6(10),800-53r5|AC-6(10),CAT|I,CCI|CCI-002235,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ITSG-33|AC-6,LEVEL|1A,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.4.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,Rule-ID|SV-257785r1044833_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-09-211050,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3,Vuln-ID|V-257785"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22008"
      cmd         : "/bin/systemctl status ctrl-alt-del.target | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"No results found\"'}"
      expect      : "(^[\\s]*Loaded:[\\s]*[Mm]asked|No results found)"
    </custom_item>
